<SEOPage title="Show only selected variant images in Shopify | VariantLens" description="Learn how to show only the product images assigned to the selected Shopify variant using a manually controlled variant gallery." eyebrow="Shopify variant galleries" heading="Show only the selected variant’s images in Shopify" intro="Give every colour or style a focused gallery instead of showing shoppers every product image at once."><h2>Why Shopify stores show unrelated variant images</h2><p>A product can contain media for several colours, materials, or styles. Depending on the theme and gallery configuration, changing the selected variant may update the featured image while leaving the rest of the product media visible.</p><h2>Organise media around the selected variant</h2><p>VariantLens lets the merchant manually assign the correct product images to each variant. Its storefront gallery reads those assignments and displays the matching set when the selection changes.</p><h2>Why manual assignment matters</h2><p>Product photography is not always named consistently, and several variants may share detail images. Manual control lets the merchant verify each set instead of depending on automatic guesses.</p><h2>A practical workflow</h2><ol><li>Select the Shopify product.</li><li>Assign its front, back, lifestyle, and detail images to each relevant variant.</li><li>Save the assignments.</li><li>Test each storefront variant before promoting the product.</li></ol></SEOPage>

